{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/r1-completeness_governance.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":579064,\"duration_api_ms\":579590,\"num_turns\":19,\"result\":\"I have all the evidence needed. Let me now produce the structured findings report.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"review_id\\\":\\\"R1-COMPLETENESS_GOVERNANCE\\\",\\\"slice\\\":\\\"WP-SCP-024 024B-core\\\",\\\"lens\\\":\\\"completeness_governance\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"APPROVED_WITH_OBSERVATIONS\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"024B-core is internally coherent under the COMPLETENESS_GOVERNANCE lens at R12. The scope-split decision is empirically justified (R6→R7→R8 trajectory documented in SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md, 'why not descope' framing explicit, extras-parking branch preserved with audit trail, carry-forward IDs named). D-044 is correctly scoped to core deliverables and cites SCOPE-CORRECTION. STATUS.md chain documents the split, outcome rows, extras-parking branch reference, and plan-doc §6 amendment. Plan-doc §6 024B row and footnote correctly gate 024C on both halves plus FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001. All five plan-doc invariant-2 check-paths map to code byte-for-byte. Scaffolder emits 4 files with substitution completeness check; template carries Renovate auto-bump marker; CI enforcement script implements all 5 cascade-status check-paths; test suites cover all 6 plan-doc worked-example matrix cases plus SAFE-003 phantom-entry test and exactly-one-match assertions. Extras carve-out is clean: no --restore, no break-glass §12.8, no .github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml. VERSIONING.md alignment correct — all new files are internal tooling; no version bump required. TF-024B-SCAFFOLDER-023E002-UPDATE and FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 are correctly filed in the 024B-core/extras section of STATUS.md. Three MIN findings: plan-doc §6 024C AC column still omits FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 as inline gate (carry-forward from R11); plan-doc §5.3 emitted-files list still omits MANIFEST.json bullet (carry-forward); TF-024B-core-WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001 is placed in the 020C.1 STATUS.md section rather than 024B-core/extras. Three nit findings: R8-CORR IDs lack inline description in SCOPE-CORRECTION (carry-forward); DISPATCH-NOTE §Sequencing cites D-040 (rule-RFC timing) for a tooling slice; DISPATCH-NOTE §Scope (out) omits FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 as a 024C gate condition alongside 024B-extras merge.\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-MIN-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Plan-doc §6 024C acceptance-criteria column does not inline FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 as a hard gate precondition for 024C opening.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"STATUS.md 2026-05-09 PM chain row 3 states '024C entry now conditional on BOTH 024B-core + 024B-extras merged + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure'. Plan-doc §6 024C AC column (line 207) lists only 'PIM required-check live; ≥1 Renovate-bump cycle clean; D-045 filed'. FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 appears only in the §6 split-note footnote (line 213) and STATUS.md. Carry-forward from R11; not in fix-round-10/11 scope boundary.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A 024C authoring operator consulting the §6 AC column as the primary reference will not see FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 as a gate. Risk of premature 024C opening if the footnote and STATUS.md are not consulted.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add 'FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closed (per STATUS.md)' to the 024C row Deliverable or AC column in plan-doc §6. Footnote and STATUS.md remain as supporting context.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-MIN-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Plan-doc §5.3 emitted-files bullet list names 3 files; the scaffolder emits 4 (MANIFEST.json is absent from §5.3).\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Plan-doc §5.3 (lines 157-164) enumerates wrapper, CODEOWNERS-snippet, CASCADE-PR-BODY.md. MANIFEST.json is documented in D-044, DISPATCH-NOTE scope table, scaffold-downstream.sh (lines 173-243), and test validate_manifest() — but not in §5.3. Carry-forward from R11.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A §5.3 reader drafting or auditing cascade slices would not know MANIFEST.json is emitted. §5.3 is the canonical scaffolder spec prose cited by future cascade slice authors; omission creates a documentation gap in the primary reference.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add a fourth bullet to §5.3: '`<output-dir>/MANIFEST.json` (SHA256 audit manifest listing emitted files + metadata per D-044 operational contract)'.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-MIN-003\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"TF-024B-core-WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001 is filed in the wrong STATUS.md section ('Tracked-forward items from 020C.1') instead of 'Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-024 024B-core / 024B-extras'.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"STATUS.md line ~175 has 'TF-024B-core-WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001: 024B-extras workflow wiring will hardcode --tooling-slice-id...' appended to the pre-existing 020C.1 TF section. The dedicated '024B-core / 024B-extras' section at line ~297 contains FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 and TF-024B-SCAFFOLDER-023E002-UPDATE but not WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001. Additionally WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001 lacks the '(open)' status parenthetical that the other 024B-core TF entries carry.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"An operator scanning STATUS.md for 024B-core tracked-forward items will find two of three in the correct section and miss WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001 because it appears under 020C.1 (a pre-existing WP-SCP-020 section). Cross-referencing is harder if the section boundary is wrong.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Move TF-024B-core-WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001 from the 020C.1 section to 'Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-024 024B-core / 024B-extras'. Add '(open)' status parenthetical to match the section format: '**TF-024B-core-WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001** (open): ...'\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-nit-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md and STATUS.md reference R8-CORR-001/002/003 by ID only, with no inline description of the defect class each ID represents.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"SCOPE-CORRECTION §'Carry-forward from extras-parking': 'informed by R8-CORR-001/002/003 carry-forward findings'. STATUS.md 2026-05-09 PM chain row 2: 'R8-CORR-001/002/003 (extras-parking r8-archive) carry forward as known findings.' Descriptions exist only in the r8-archive on the extras-parking branch. Carry-forward from R11.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"024B-extras authoring operator must locate and read the parking branch r8-archive to understand the carry-forward findings. Minor friction; branch and archive are correctly preserved.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add one-line description per ID in SCOPE-CORRECTION §'Carry-forward': e.g. 'R8-CORR-001: <defect class>; R8-CORR-002: <defect class>; R8-CORR-003: <defect class>'. Keeps the authoring context self-contained without requiring archive lookup.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-nit-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE §Sequencing row 5 cites 'self-merge per D-040'; D-040 governs rule-RFC proposal timing (48h CEILING vs FLOOR), which does not apply to tooling slices.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE §Sequencing: '| 5 | R-fixpoint + self-merge per D-040 | Opus | ~10 min |'. D-040 (DECISIONS.md line ~88) amends rule-RFC process: 'Operator may merge as soon as adversarial review reaches fixpoint AND the proposal PR is open with the scp-rule-proposal label applied.' 024B-core has no scp-rule-proposal label and is not an RFC. Self-merge authority for tooling slices derives from D-031 (single-operator mode) + general dispatch protocol.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Incorrect decision citation; could mislead future operator checking under what authority a tooling slice self-merge proceeds. D-031 is the correct authority.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Change 'per D-040' to 'per D-031 (single-operator mode)' in DISPATCH-NOTE §Sequencing row 5.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"CG-nit-003\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE §Scope (out) omits FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 as a 024C prerequisite alongside '024B-extras merges'.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE §Scope (out): '024C PIM cascade kickoff. Unblocked when 024B-extras merges.' No mention of FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001. Plan-doc §6 footnote (line 213) and STATUS.md 024B-core/extras TF section correctly document the three-gate condition: 024B-core + 024B-extras + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"An operator reading only DISPATCH-NOTE §Scope (out) as the 024C trigger sees only 024B-extras merge as the gate. Low risk since STATUS.md is the authoritative TF reference and FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 has '024C MUST NOT open until closed' explicitly.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Append 'AND FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closed (STATUS.md)' to the 024C scope-out line in DISPATCH-NOTE for completeness.\\\"}],\\\"crit_count\\\":0,\\\"maj_count\\\":0,\\\"min_count\\\":3,\\\"nit_count\\\":3,\\\"approved\\\":true}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"a55c606f-65ac-4e14-89d5-21f0e49ebb7f\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.2556218,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":21940,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":126574,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":912451,\"output_tokens\":29326,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":126574,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":6362,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":131697,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2258,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2258},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inpu