ble.\" \"\" --allow-not-applicable\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:742:  run_case \"$repo_dir\" 2 '' \"ERROR: --allow-not-applicable requires DISPATCH-NOTE to declare 'slice-type: tooling'. Found: cohort. Cohort cascade slices (024C/D/E/F) MUST NOT pass --allow-not-applicable.\" \"\" --allow-not-applicable --tooling-slice-id 024C\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:752:  run_case \"$repo_dir\" 2 '' 'ERROR: --allow-not-applicable requires --tooling-slice-id <id> where <id> ∈ {024A, 024B-core, 024B-extras, 024G}' \"\" --allow-not-applicable --tooling-slice-id 024C\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:772:  run_case \"$repo_dir\" 2 '' \"ERROR: --allow-not-applicable was passed but cascade-status is 'onboarded'\" \"\" --allow-not-applicable\ntests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh:132:  # pyyaml is optional in some environments; skip the lint check cleanly\ntests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh:134:  python3 -c 'import yaml' 2>/dev/null || { echo 'SKIP: pyyaml not installed; YAML validation skipped'; return 0; }\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:3:**Last Updated:** 2026-05-09 (D-044 filed for WP-SCP-024 024B-core; estate cascade scope split)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:29:> **D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reservation note (2026-05-03, plan-doc 024A):**\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:30:> D-044 was reserved for WP-SCP-024 slice 024B (`scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh`\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:44:> assign D-044, D-045, or D-046 to any other decision filed during that\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:86:| D-038 | 2026-05-02 | Adopt hash-pinned Python supply-chain installs across the SCP federation primitive's two YAML/JSON-validating workflows (`.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` × 4 install sites, `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` × 1 install site) via `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/policy-check.txt`. Top-level pins (`pyyaml==6.0.2` + `jsonschema==4.23.0`) match the prior inline pins exactly — no version bump on the public Python deps; only the install mechanism is hardened. Lockfile generated by `pip-compile --generate-hashes` from `requirements/policy-check.in`; full transitive closure (`attrs`, `jsonschema-specifications`, `referencing`, `rpds-py`) hash-pinned with all-platform wheel SHA256s. Closes WP-SCP-022 TF-020H3rg-002 (filed at 020H.3 R1 safety MIN-SAFE-006 — a PyPI compromise of either pinned version could substitute a malicious package on the next install; `--require-hashes` causes pip to refuse install when the served wheel's SHA256 is not in the lockfile). PATCH bump (v1.0.0 → v1.0.1) per `policies/VERSIONING.md` PATCH category (\"internal refactors of helpers/lib\"); no `policies/deprecations.yaml` entry required (no surface deprecation, no behaviour change for adopters). Lockfile regeneration command captured in `requirements/policy-check.txt` header AND `requirements/policy-check.in` documentation block | ACCEPTED | Symmetric supply-chain hardening with the pre-existing `scripts/scp-policy-check.lock` (OPA + Conftest + Regal binary SHA256 verification) and Sigstore attestation soft-warn for OPA (TF-007). All three layers — Python deps, OPA-family binaries, GitHub Actions SHA pins — are now hash-anchored at SCP source. The lockfile + `.in` source pair mirrors `scripts/.tool-versions` + `scripts/scp-policy-check.lock` (input + lockfile pattern). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged for lockfile regeneration: an operator who regenerates without re-reviewing the pip-compile output could introduce drifted transitive versions; mitigation is the `requirements/policy-check.in` source-of-truth (pins only the top-level deps; transitive resolution is automatic but reviewable in the diff). Future upgrades to `pyyaml` / `jsonschema` itself follow the same path: edit `.in`, regenerate `.txt`, review diff. The Sigstore re-tightening (TF-007) is parallel work on a different supply-chain dimension. Identified at 020H.3 R1 safety MIN-SAFE-006 closure |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:87:| D-039 | 2026-05-02 | Extend the slice 020M hash-pinned Python supply-chain install pattern to the SCP-self conflict-gate workflow (`.github/workflows/conflict-gate.yml` \"Install Python dependencies\" step) per WP-SCP-022 slice 020N, closing TF-020M-001. New `requirements/conflict-gate.in` (top-level pins matching `pyproject.toml` `[project.dependencies]` + `[project.optional-dependencies.dev]`: fastapi, uvicorn, httpx, jsonschema, pydantic, pyyaml, pytest, ruff, mypy) + generated `requirements/conflict-gate.txt` (pip-compile --generate-hashes under Python 3.12 to match `setup-python: python-version: \"3.12\"`; full transitive closure with all-platform wheel SHA256s). Install pattern: (i) `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/conflict-gate.txt` (PyPI deps); (ii) `pip install --no-deps vendor/python/ct_auth-0.8.0-py3-none-any.whl` (local vendored wheel — not on PyPI; CODEOWNERS-protected via `vendor/** @jrnb2024`); (iii) `pip install --no-deps -e .` (editable local SCP package without re-resolving deps already hash-verified in step (i)); (iv) post-install version-pin assertion (`assert yaml.__version__ == \"6.0.3\"; assert jsonschema.__version__ == \"4.26.0\"; assert fastapi.__version__ == \"0.136.1\"; assert pydantic.VERSION == \"2.13.3\"`) defending against future-PR drift (mirrors 020M SAFE-MAJ-002 pattern). Deliberate pyyaml-version drift accepted: conflict-gate.txt resolves pyyaml==6.0.3, policy-check.txt pins pyyaml==6.0.2 — independent workflows with independent supply-chain anchors; both hash-anchored. **No semver bump.** Per `policies/VERSIONING.md` §\"Scope\", `conflict-gate.yml` is not in the public-surface enumeration (workflow_call inputs on `policy-check.yml`, schema contracts, rule IDs); it is a SCP-self-only workflow that adopters do not consume. Therefore no `policies/deprecations.yaml` entry, no version-manifest bump, no release notes — internal hardening | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-038 (slice 020M hash-pinning of policy-check.yml + release-gate.yml). The conflict-gate is the third Python-installing workflow in the SCP repo; closing the unhardened install completes the Python supply-chain hardening across all three SCP-self workflows that pip-install at runtime. Threat surface (PyPI compromise of conflict-gate's deps) was acknowledged at 020M R1 safety as MIN-class because conflict-gate is SCP-self-only (not adopter-facing); a compromise would degrade SCP self's policy-evaluator quality but not directly compromise adopters. The user's directive to clear all outstanding TFs (rather than defer to v1.1 maintenance) raised this from forward-compat to in-flight closure. The `--no-deps` editable install of the local SCP package is the tradeoff: pip refuses `--require-hashes` on editable installs, so the local source tree is installed without re-resolving (its PyPI deps are already hash-verified above). The `ct-auth` vendored wheel is similarly outside `--require-hashes` (pip refuses for local file: URLs); chain-of-trust is the `vendor/**` CODEOWNERS coverage + the wheel being in-tree (no network fetch). Identified at 020M R1 safety SAFE-MIN-003 closure |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:92:| D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-core operational contracts for cascade scaffolding. Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (`SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically - bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits a TF-023E-002 warning for post-v1.2.0 SHAs while recommending the v1.0.0 pin; `--scp-sha` 40-char hex regex; `--default-branch` enum {main, master, develop}; `--scorecard-emit` enum; `--output-dir` writability + path-normalised system-path denylist (incl `/private/var/*` macOS canonicalisation); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments per plan-doc §5.3. Canonical adopter slugs are normalization aids only, not collision-resistant IDs, so cohort repo names must remain unique after canonicalization. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12 with Renovate inline-comment marker `# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane` enabling auto-bump per plan-doc invariant 8 Threshold A criterion; substitutions `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`, `{{SCP_SHA}}`, `{{SCORECARD_EMIT}}`; least-privilege workflow-level permissions (`contents:read` + `statuses:write` only). (3) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CLI tool implements plan-doc invariant 2 cascade-status CI enforcement: 4 enforcement behaviours (fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised; `onboarded` -> log-entry-modified + target-match; `onboarded-operator-bump` -> log entry + `STATUS.md` `TF-024X-renovate-<slug>` row matching invariant 2 regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` -> `DISPATCH-NOTE` `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference + log file NOT modified) + explicit tooling-slice opt-in gate for `cascade-status: not applicable` (`--allow-not-applicable`; default refusal for direct CLI use). Regex via `python3 re.search()` (PCRE-style); exactly-one-match assertions on both `cascade-status` and `**Target:**` extraction close multi-occurrence injection bypasses; adopter-slug canonicalisation per plan-doc spec. CLI tool only - GitHub Actions workflow wiring (`.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`) defers to slice 024B-extras alongside `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure. D-044 was reserved for slice 024B at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04); after the operator-decided scope-split (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md), D-044 stays scoped to core deliverables; sibling D-NNN may be reserved at 024B-extras authoring time for the deferred surface (`--restore` + break-glass + workflow wiring). Slice 024B-core ships under documented protocol deviation per feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md note + justify rule (kernel hook lives in ACC repo only; per-repo install pattern is FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 - open). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge per the §9 reservation block. The original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds against a single branch with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code (R6 missed primary-deliverable workflow wiring; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR). Empirical signal: surface area too large (16 files, ~3500 lines added) for single-pass convergence. Operator decided 2026-05-09 to split 024B into 024B-core (this slice; ~5 files; scaffolder + template + CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (deferred; `--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope - both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens. Original 024B work preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` branch (audit trail: 7 codex-fix-round-N-audit.log files + 7 R-round archive directories incl r8-archive carry-forward findings). Slice 024B-core scope is internally coherent: scaffolder generates adopter artefacts; CI enforcement script (CLI) validates cascade-status declarations; tests cover both. The CLI script can be invoked manually as a stop-gap until 024B-extras wires it into GitHub Actions. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation |\nSTATUS.md:119:| 6 | #102 | **024A** | WP-SCP-024 plan-doc v0.1 — estate cascade. Defines adopter cohort `{pim, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower}` (per D-035) explicitly **FLA-independent** per operator direction; canary-first sequencing PIM → control-tower → mapp-doc-agent + recommender → shopify-app; per-adopter onboarding contract (adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice + invocation log + post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle). Reserves D-044/D-045/D-046 for implementation slices 024B/024C/024G. Threshold A: ≥3 of 5 cohort adopters required-check live + ≥1 SCP minor version-bump propagated cleanly via Renovate + USER-GATE-E signed. Required-check cascade is primary deliverable; scorecard-emit opt-in is secondary follow-up gated on TF-023E-002 closure, and 024B-core now warns on post-v1.2.0 SHAs while keeping the v1.0.0 pin as the operational fallback until TF-023E-002 closes. **Cascade-status spec hardened over 9 review rounds** (32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds — unprecedented; cause was the cascade-status / CI-enforcement clause being structurally cross-cutting): 3 close-states (`onboarded`, `onboarded-operator-bump`, `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`) × 4 CI behaviours (3 named + fail-closed default) × (positive evidence + machine-enforceable regex format spec + negative assertion). WP-SCP-024 is the natural successor to the 5-move MVCP — turns SCP's estate observability (WP-SCP-023) into action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\nSTATUS.md:147:| 1 | Slice 024B-core: `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` + `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` + `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` (CLI) + `tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh` + `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh` (cascade-status enforcement only). D-044 filed scoped to core. Branch: `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-core`. |\nSTATUS.md:175:- **TF-024B-core-WORKFLOW-MITIGATION-001**: 024B-extras workflow wiring will hardcode `--tooling-slice-id` per workflow file and omit `--allow-not-applicable` from cohort workflows, closing the residual operator-supplied slice-id bypass surface. 024B-core keeps the CLI guard + documentation only.\nSTATUS.md:202:- ~~**TF-020H3rg-002**: `pip install --require-hashes` for `policy-check.yml` + `release-gate.yml` pyyaml/jsonschema installs.~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020M** (this PR's branch). `requirements/policy-check.in` (top-level pins) + `requirements/policy-check.txt` (generated by `pip-compile --generate-hashes`, full transitive closure with all-platform wheel SHA256s) added. All 5 install sites (4× `policy-check.yml` + 1× `release-gate.yml`) switched to `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/policy-check.txt`. Top-level pins unchanged from v1.0.0 (`pyyaml==6.0.2` + `jsonschema==4.23.0`); only the install mechanism is hardened. PATCH bump v1.0.0 → v1.0.1 per VERSIONING.md \"internal refactors\". D-038 filed.\nSTATUS.md:208:- ~~**TF-020M-001**: `conflict-gate.yml` retains `pip install pyyaml>=6.0` (line ~42) without hash-pinning.~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020N** (this PR's branch). `requirements/conflict-gate.in` (top-level pins matching `pyproject.toml` `[project.dependencies]` + `[project.optional-dependencies.dev]`) + `requirements/conflict-gate.txt` (generated by `pip-compile --generate-hashes` under Python 3.12, full transitive closure with all-platform wheel SHA256s) added. `.github/workflows/conflict-gate.yml` \"Install Python dependencies\" step restructured to: (i) hash-pinned `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/conflict-gate.txt`; (ii) local vendored `ct-auth` wheel installed `--no-deps`; (iii) editable local SCP package installed `--no-deps`; (iv) post-install version-pin assertion (mirrors 020M SAFE-MAJ-002 pattern). No semver bump (conflict-gate is internal-only per VERSIONING.md §\"Scope\"). D-039 filed.\nSTATUS.md:297:## Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-024 024B-core / 024B-extras\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:14:# docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md; docs/DECISIONS.md D-044.\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:20:Usage: check-invocation-log-entry.sh --pr <number> | --diff-base <ref> --dispatch-note <path> [--status-md <path>] [--branch-protection-log <path>] [--allow-not-applicable] [--tooling-slice-id <id>]\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:31:  --allow-not-applicable         Allow cascade-status: not applicable.\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:32:  --tooling-slice-id <id>        Required with --allow-not-applicable; must be one of 024A, 024B-core, 024B-extras, 024G.\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:77:    --allow-not-applicable)\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:81:    --tooling-slice-id)\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:82:      [ $# -ge 2 ] || die \"ERROR: --tooling-slice-id requires a value\" 2\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:206:      die \"ERROR: cascade-status: not applicable found, but --allow-not-applicable was not passed. This carve-out is for tooling slices ONLY (024A, 024B-core, 024B-extras, 024G); cohort cascade slices 024C/D/E/F MUST NOT use it. If this is a tooling slice, pass --allow-not-applicable explicitly.\" 2\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:209:      die \"ERROR: --allow-not-applicable requires DISPATCH-NOTE to declare 'slice-type: tooling'. Found: ${slice_type}. Cohort cascade slices (024C/D/E/F) MUST NOT pass --allow-not-applicable.\" 2\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:213:      *) die \"ERROR: --allow-not-applicable requires --tooling-slice-id <id> where <id> ∈ {024A, 024B-core, 024B-extras, 024G}\" 2 ;;\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:219:    die \"FAIL-CLOSED: cascade-status field absent or unrecognised; must be one of {onboarded, onboarded-operator-bump, blocked-on-adopter-conflict}; not applicable requires --allow-not-applicable for tooling slices only\" 2\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:224:  die \"ERROR: --allow-not-applicable was passed but cascade-status is '$cascade_status' — flag is for tooling slices declaring cascade-status: not applicable ONLY. Cohort cascade slices (024C/D/E/F) MUST NOT pass this flag.\" 2\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:233:    die \"ERROR: --tooling-slice-id requires DISPATCH-NOTE to declare 'slice-type: tooling'. Found: ${slice_type}. Cohort cascade slices (024C/D/E/F) MUST NOT pass --tooling-slice-id.\" 2\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:237:    *) die \"ERROR: --tooling-slice-id requires one of {024A, 024B-core, 024B-extras, 024G}\" 2 ;;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
