{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_93","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS.md | sed -n '92,96p'\"","aggregated_output":"    92\t| D-042 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard aggregator pipeline trust model per WP-SCP-023 023C (this PR). Mechanism: per-emit verification via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow <expected_workflow_ref>` (the GitHub Actions Artifact Attestation OIDC pattern, mandatory per the D-042 reservation note above + 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure); index trust rooted in git's required-signed-commits (slice 020J) + `output/scorecards/** @jrnb2024` CODEOWNERS coverage (slice 023A) + branch protection on main (slice 020D2), NOT a separate Ed25519 key layer. The aggregator runs as `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` on a weekly cron (Monday 06:00 UTC) + `workflow_dispatch`; two-job structure (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped via job-level permissions, mirroring the 023B `attest-scorecard` job split); reads `docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml` (CODEOWNERS-protected at `docs/scorecards/**`), pulls each adopter's latest green policy-check run's `scorecard-emit.json` artifact, verifies attestation, schema-validates emit, aggregates into `output/scorecards/index.json` (schema: `schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json`), and opens a PR for operator review. Failure modes (verification_failure / unreachable / no_emit) record loudly per-adopter — never silently dropped. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema `additionalProperties: false` at every level). Internal-only workflow per `policies/VERSIONING.md` §\"Scope\" (mirrors 020N conflict-gate.yml posture); no semver bump. Verifies WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 6 (\"Aggregator output is Ed25519-signed\") in spirit — Sigstore/Fulcio uses Ed25519 under the hood, managed by GitHub rather than by an SCP-side private key, eliminating the private-key-distribution surface | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-041 (per-emit data shape + opt-in model) — D-041 ratified the EMITTER side of the trust model; D-042 ratifies the AGGREGATOR / VERIFIER side. The mandatory `--signer-workflow` constraint was already pre-committed at the D-042 reservation note above (closes 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001) — this slice ratifies it as workflow code. The Ed25519-via-Sigstore framing eliminates the chicken-and-egg of \"where does the SCP private key live and how does the aggregator hold it without exposing adopters\" — GitHub manages the keys via OIDC + Sigstore. The two-job permission split (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped) is identical to 023B's `policy-check` + `attest-scorecard` split (closes the analogous threat surface where workflow-level write permissions could be exploited by a compromised aggregate-side step). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: aggregator runs on the SCP repo with single-operator identity (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-042 reservation + 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure |\n    93\t| D-043 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report (`docs/scorecards/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`) + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` — per WP-SCP-023 023D (this PR). Markdown generator at `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` produces deterministic golden-file-tested output reading `output/scorecards/index.json`; aggregator workflow `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` extended in the commit job to invoke the generator + add the rendered markdown to the operator-review PR alongside the index. MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` (registered in `src/standards_control_plane/mcp_server/tools.py`): read-only contract per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 5; request shape `{repo_filter?, since_emitted_at?}`; response shape excludes waiver content (`reason` / `approved_by` / `waiver_id` — invariant 2) by Pydantic model construction (extra=forbid + explicit field whitelist). The MCP method reads `output/scorecards/index.json` from the SCP repo working copy at call time; staleness is observable via the response's `aggregated_at` field. ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 documents the adopter onboarding workflow. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by Pydantic models + schema + dedicated pytest scans on both markdown + MCP responses) | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-041 + D-042 — D-043 ratifies the CONSUMER side: markdown for operators/auditors, MCP for agents/tooling. Read-only contract + Pydantic-enforced field whitelist + golden-file pytest together preserve invariant 2 across both surfaces. The MCP method does NOT introduce a new authentication primitive — it rides on WP-SCP-021's existing Ed25519 receipt mechanism (consult-class semantics). The markdown report is informational and CODEOWNERS-protected via `docs/scorecards/** @jrnb2024`; operators can hand-edit before merging the aggregator PR if needed (regenerator overwrites on next run). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the MCP server runs at acc.brokapps.ai; if down, agents lose `consult_scorecard` access but the markdown report + git index remain consultable. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-043 reservation |\n    94\t| D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-core operational contracts for cascade scaffolding. Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (`SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically - bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits a TF-023E-002 warning for post-v1.2.0 SHAs while recommending the v1.0.0 pin; `--scp-sha` 40-char hex regex; `--default-branch` enum {main, master, develop}; `--scorecard-emit` enum; `--output-dir` writability + path-normalised system-path denylist (incl `/private/var/*` macOS canonicalisation); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments per plan-doc §5.3. Canonical adopter slugs are normalization aids only, not collision-resistant IDs, so cohort repo names must remain unique after canonicalization. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12 with Renovate inline-comment marker `# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane` enabling auto-bump per plan-doc invariant 8 Threshold A criterion; substitutions `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`, `{{SCP_SHA}}`, `{{SCORECARD_EMIT}}`; least-privilege workflow-level permissions (`contents:read` + `statuses:write` only). (3) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CLI tool implements plan-doc invariant 2 cascade-status CI enforcement: 4 enforcement behaviours (fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised; `onboarded` -> log-entry-modified + target-match; `onboarded-operator-bump` -> log entry + `STATUS.md` `TF-024X-renovate-<slug>` row matching invariant 2 regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` -> `DISPATCH-NOTE` `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference + log file NOT modified) + explicit tooling-slice opt-in gate for `cascade-status: not applicable` (`--allow-not-applicable`; default refusal for direct CLI use). Regex via `python3 re.search()` (PCRE-style); exactly-one-match assertions on both `cascade-status` and `**Target:**` extraction close multi-occurrence injection bypasses; adopter-slug canonicalisation per plan-doc spec. CLI tool only - GitHub Actions workflow wiring (`.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`) defers to slice 024B-extras alongside `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure. D-044 was reserved for slice 024B at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04); after the operator-decided scope-split (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md), D-044 stays scoped to core deliverables; sibling D-NNN may be reserved at 024B-extras authoring time for the deferred surface (`--restore` + break-gl